<section id="about" class="section">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="heading-accent">01. About Me</p>
      <h2 class="heading">Systems thinking. <span>Hands-on work.</span></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-12 items-start">
      <!-- Text Content -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-4 reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.1s;">
        <p class="text-slate leading-relaxed">
          I'm a Systems Administrator whose work spans <span class="text-accent">infrastructure, automation, and software development</span>.
          DevOps is a substantial part of that work: using infrastructure as code, building CI/CD workflows, and making
          deployments repeatable and easier to maintain. As the <span class="text-accent">owner of CK Technology LLC</span>,
          I bring that approach to business IT, from secure networks and cloud services to the day-to-day work of keeping
          systems running. Previously, I worked as a <span class="text-accent">Systems Administrator at Resolve Technology</span>.
        </p>

        <p class="text-slate leading-relaxed">
          I've spent <span class="text-accent">7+ years</span> working across systems administration, network security,
          and cloud infrastructure, driven by a curiosity about how systems work under the hood. That curiosity also
          led me into software development, where I can build tools for the problems I encounter in operations.
          I hold a <span class="text-accent">B.S. in Software Development from SNHU</span>.
        </p>

        <p class="text-slate leading-relaxed">
          Outside of client work, I spend much of my time working with <span class="text-accent">Linux and open-source software</span>,
          contributing to projects and building tools in Python, Rust, and Go that make everyday operations easier. My lab gives me room to
          experiment with infrastructure, automation, and local AI workflows, and to understand how the pieces fit
          together. I enjoy getting under the hood, solving problems, and turning what I learn into systems I can
          maintain and improve over time.
        </p>

      </div>

      <!-- Profile Image -->
      <div class="reveal flex justify-center md:justify-end" style="transition-delay: 0.2s;">
        <div class="relative group">
          <!-- Decorative border -->
          <div class="absolute inset-0 border-2 border-accent rounded-lg translate-x-4 translate-y-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:translate-y-2"></div>

          <!-- Image container -->
          <div class="relative w-64 h-64 md:w-72 md:h-72 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-accent/10">
            <img
              src="/profile.jpg"
              alt="Christopher Kelley"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-500"
            />
            <!-- Overlay -->
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-accent/20 hover:bg-transparent transition-colors duration-300"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
